 ],
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "hero-01",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Iʿrāb in the Qur'an. Ten verses.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-02",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "These are real verses. Each one has a past verb and a naṣb noun.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "sub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-03",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "They also use the rafʿ and jarr rules we already know.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-04",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Same colours. Same method.",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-title-01",
   "scene": "c01-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter one. Three small notes for these verses.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-01",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "First note. Attached pronouns are fixed.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-02",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "His, her and your can be short endings. They join the noun before them.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-03",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "They are the owner.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-04",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "We split them off, so you can see the noun's ending. Take his Lord.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-05",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "رَبَّهُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-06",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "His is the small piece at the end.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-07",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Second note. A past verb can hide its doer.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-08",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "An order verb hides the word you. In the same way, a past verb can hide the word he.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-09",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "(هُوَ)",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-10",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It can also hide the word she.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-11",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "(هِيَ)",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-12",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "This verb means she tore.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-13",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "قَدَّتْ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-14",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The ending of this verb tells us the doer is she.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-15",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Third note. Some names never take tanween.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-16",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "آدَمُ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-17",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "سُلَيْمَانُ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-18",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "دَاوُودَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-19",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "One damma or one fatha only.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-20",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "But names like Nuh do take tanween.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-notes-21",
   "scene": "c01-notes",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "نُوحٌ",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-also-01",
   "scene": "c01-also",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Also. Some past verbs end in a letter with sukūn, like the verb in the second note.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "show"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-also-02",
   "scene": "c01-also",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Before al, that last letter takes a small kasra, just like an order verb.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-also-03",
   "scene": "c01-also",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "She closed the doors.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-also-04",
   "scene": "c01-also",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "غَلَّقَتِ الأَبْوَابَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-also-05",
   "scene": "c01-also",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It is still fixed.",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-title-01",
   "scene": "c02-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter two. The colour key.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-key-01",
   "scene": "c02-key",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Navy is the verb. Past and order verbs are fixed.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "key:verb"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-key-02",
   "scene": "c02-key",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Orange is the doer. Who did the action? It takes rafʿ.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "key:doer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-key-03",
   "scene": "c02-key",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The next four jobs all take naṣb.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-key-04",
   "scene": "c02-key",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Pink is the object. What? Whom?",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "key:obj"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-key-05",
   "scene": "c02-key",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Teal is the purpose. Why?",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "key:purp"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-key-06",
   "scene": "c02-key",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Brown is time or place. When? Where? With no preposition.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "key:when"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-key-07",
   "scene": "c02-key",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Olive is the state. How?",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "key:state"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-key-08",
   "scene": "c02-key",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The small boxes from last lesson still work. After a preposition. Ownership. Adjective. And after wa.",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "old"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-title-01",
   "scene": "c03-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter three. The ten verses.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-title-02",
   "scene": "c03-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Read each verse aloud with your teacher first. Then solve the cards. Every ending is missing.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "sub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-overview-01",
   "scene": "c03-overview",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Each row is one verse. Next to it are its reference and the jobs inside it.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-overview-02",
   "scene": "c03-overview",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Most of them are a short piece of a longer verse.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "rows"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-overview-03",
   "scene": "c03-overview",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "On screen, they are written in our usual spelling.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-overview-04",
   "scene": "c03-overview",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The naṣb noun is an object, a time, or a state.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-overview-05",
   "scene": "c03-overview",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "For each verse, we first hear its meaning. Then we hear it recited.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-overview-06",
   "scene": "c03-overview",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "After that, we box it together, piece by piece.",
   "pause": 0.8,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "v01-01",
   "scene": "v01",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Verse one. From Surah Ta-Ha. And Adam disobeyed his Lord.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "en"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v01-02",
   "scene": "v01",
   "lang": "qr",
   "text": "وَعَصَى آدَمُ رَبَّهُ",
   "pause": 0.8,
   "cues": [
    "sentence",
    "recite"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v01-03",
   "scene": "v01",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "First, the verb. Disobeyed. It is a past verb, so it is fixed.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "group:0",
    "line:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v01-04",
   "scene": "v01",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The wa before it means and. It is a particle. It never changes.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "line:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v01-05",
   "scene": "v01",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Who disobeyed?",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ask:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v01-06",
   "scene": "v01",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "آدَمُ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "group:1",
    "vowel:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v01-07",
   "scene": "v01",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Adam. He is the doer, so he takes rafʿ, with damma.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "line:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v01-08",
   "scene": "v01",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Only one damma, no tanween. Some names never take tanween.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "v01-09",
   "scene": "v01",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Whom did he disobey?",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ask:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v01-10",
   "scene": "v01",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "رَبَّهُ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "group:2",
    "vowel:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v01-11",
   "scene": "v01",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "His Lord. That is the object, so it takes naṣb. Its sign is fatha.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "line:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v01-12",
   "scene": "v01",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "His is an attached pronoun at the end of the word. It is the owner, and it is fixed.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "line:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v01-13",
   "scene": "v01",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Because Lord is owned, it has no tanween. Just one fatha.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "v01-14",
   "scene": "v01",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Listen to the verse once more.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "v01-15",
   "scene": "v01",
   "lang": "qr",
   "text": "وَعَصَى آدَمُ رَبَّهُ",
   "pause": 0.9,
   "cues": [
    "recite"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02-01",
   "scene": "v02",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Verse two. From Surah Hud. And Nuh called out to his son.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "en"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02-02",
   "scene": "v02",
   "lang": "qr",
   "text": "وَنَادَى نُوحٌ ابْنَهُ",
   "pause": 0.8,
   "cues": [
    "sentence",
    "recite"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02-03",
   "scene": "v02",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "First, the verb. Called out. It is a past verb, so it is fixed.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "group:0",
    "line:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02-04",
   "scene": "v02",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The wa before it is a particle. It never changes.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "line:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02-05",
   "scene": "v02",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Who called out?",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ask:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02-06",
   "scene": "v02",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "نُوحٌ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "group:1",
    "vowel:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02-07",
   "scene": "v02",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Nuh. He is the doer, so he takes rafʿ, with damma.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "line:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02-08",
   "scene": "v02",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "This name does take tanween. Damma with tanween.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "v02-09",
   "scene": "v02",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Whom did he call?",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ask:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02-10",
   "scene": "v02",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "ابْنَهُ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "group:2",
    "vowel:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02-11",
   "scene": "v02",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "His son. In English we say called out to his son. The Arabic has no extra word.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "v02-12",
   "scene": "v02",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "So it is the object. It takes naṣb. Its sign is fatha.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "line:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02-13",
   "scene": "v02",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "His is the attached pronoun. It is the owner, and it is fixed.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "line:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02-14",
   "scene": "v02",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Son is owned, so no tanween. Just one fatha.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "v03-01",
   "scene": "v03",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Verse three. From Surah An-Naml. And Sulayman inherited from Dawud.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "en"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03-02",
   "scene": "v03",
   "lang": "qr",
   "text": "وَوَرِثَ سُلَيْمَانُ دَاوُودَ",
   "pause": 0.8,
   "cues": [
    "sentence",
    "recite"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03-03",
   "scene": "v03",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "First, the verb. Inherited. It is a past verb, so it is fixed.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "group:0",
    "line:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03-04",
   "scene": "v03",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The wa before it is a particle. It never changes.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "line:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03-05",
   "scene": "v03",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Who inherited?",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ask:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03-06",
   "scene": "v03",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "سُلَيْمَانُ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "group:1",
    "vowel:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03-07",
   "scene": "v03",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Sulayman. He is the doer, so he takes rafʿ, with damma.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "line:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03-08",
   "scene": "v03",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Only one damma. This name never takes tanween.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "v03-09",
   "scene": "v03",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Whom did he inherit from?",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ask:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03-10",
   "scene": "v03",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "دَاوُودَ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "group:2",
    "vowel:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03-11",
   "scene": "v03",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Dawud. In English we say from Dawud. The Arabic has no extra word.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "v03-12",
   "scene": "v03",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "He is the object, so he takes naṣb, with fatha.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "line:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03-13",
   "scene": "v03",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Only one fatha. Like Adam, this name never takes tanween.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "v04-01",
   "scene": "v04",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Verse four. From Surah Yusuf. And she closed the doors.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "en"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v04-02",
